<title>SWEDEN: Atlas Copco Q3 sales fell, profit flat.</title>
<headline>Atlas Copco Q3 sales fell, profit flat.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atlas Copco said its invoiced sales in the third quarter of 1996 fell to 5.94 billion crowns from 6.08 billion in the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Operating profit after depreciation was 632 million against 619 million, and profit after financial items 665 million against 659 million.</p>
<p>Profit margin in the quarter improved to 11.2 percent from the previous year's 10.8 percent, but net profit fell to 397 million crowns from 450 million, corresponding to 2.17 crowns per share after 2.45.</p>
<p>The decrease reflected higher tax charges, it said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
